      "verification": {
        "verified": false,
        "reason": "no_user",
        "payload": "tree 561ed41be1bd382e2e4b71146e970473b0382792\nparent fabf5c52ccba619060610f3da181802c3b193478\nauthor MarcoFalke <*~=`'#}+{/-|&$^_@721217.xyz> 1793019322 +0100\ncommitter MarcoFalke <*~=`'#}+{/-|&$^_@721217.xyz> 1793019536 +0100\n\ntest: Use single node in mempool_reorg.py\n\nThe test used two nodes, which is confusing:\n\n* node[0] uses immediate tx relay via noban@127.0.0.1; However, this\n  will only apply to incoming connections, not to outgoing ones.\n* The second test requires a peer without immediate tx relay, so it\n  would be cleaner to not have any global setting for faster tx relay\n  here.\n* Two nodes is not required for testing here. Creating and submitting\n  forks, or p2p connections can be done with Python helpers.\n\nUsing a single node also allows to remove a bunch of sync and connect\ncalls.\n",
